body:
To be a bit more concrete, I propose something like:

In SVG (don't have to care about here):

```
[Exposed=Window]
interface SVGAElement : SVGGraphicsElement {
};
SVGAElement includes SVGURIReference;
SVGAElement includes HTMLOrSVGAnchorElement;
SVGAElement includes HTMLHyperlinkElementUtils;

Interface mixin SVGURIReference
{
    [SameObject, PutForwards=baseVal] readonly attribute SVGAnimatedString href;
    stringifier;
};
```

In HTML (changes needed here)

```
[Exposed=Window, HTMLConstructor]
interface HTMLAnchorElement : HTMLElement {
};
HTMLAnchorElement includes HTMLURIReference;
HTMLAnchorElement includes HTMLOrSVGAnchorElement;
HTMLAnchorElement includes HTMLHyperlinkElementUtils;

Interface mixin HTMLURIReference
{
  [CEReactions] stringifier attribute USVString href;
};

Interface mixin HTMLOrSVGAnchorElement
{
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString target;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString download;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString ping;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString rel;
  [SameObject, PutForwards=value] readonly attribute DOMTokenList relList;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString hreflang;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString type;

  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString text;

  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString referrerPolicy;
};

interface mixin HTMLHyperlinkElementUtils {
  readonly attribute USVString origin;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString protocol;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString username;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString password;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString host;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString hostname;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString port;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString pathname;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString search;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString hash;
};
```

Of course. HTMLAreaElement shares everything except `hreflang`, `type`, and `text`, so perhaps they should be split into two mixins so that area can be included too.

We can ignore animVal as it just mirrors baseVal, so as long as reflecting to baseVal works then we're good to go. 

HTMLAreaElement is currently:

```
[Exposed=Window,
 HTMLConstructor]
interface HTMLAreaElement : HTMLElement {
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString alt;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString coords;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString shape;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString target;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString download;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString ping;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString rel;
  [SameObject, PutForwards=value] readonly attribute DOMTokenList relList;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString referrerPolicy;
};
HTMLAreaElement includes HTMLHyperlinkElementUtils;
```

I just chose HTMLURIReference as it matches SVG, but I can also change SVG to use `SVGHyperlinkElementUtils` if that is the way HTML goes.


Yeah, HTMLAreaElement would just be:

```
[Exposed=Window,
 HTMLConstructor]
interface HTMLAreaElement : HTMLElement {
  ...removed members for brevity
};
HTMLAreaElement includes HTMLURIReference/HTMLHyperlinkElementUtils/Whatever;
HTMLAreaElement includes HTMLHyperlinkElementUtils;
```

OR if SVGAElement/HTMLAnchorElement/HTMLAreaElement can share a mixin it would be something like:

```
[Exposed=Window,
 HTMLConstructor]
interface HTMLAreaElement : HTMLElement {
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString alt;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString coords;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString shape;
};
HTMLAreaElement includes HTMLOrSVGHyperlinkElement;
HTMLAreaElement includes HTMLHyperlinkElementUtils; // the one with href
HTMLAreaElement includes HTMLOrSVGHyperlinkElementUtils; // existing mixin without href

interface mixin HTMLOrSVGHyperlinkElement {
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString target;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString download;
  [CEReactions] attribute USVString ping;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString rel;
  [SameObject, PutForwards=value] readonly attribute DOMTokenList relList;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString referrerPolicy;
};

// only on HTMLAnchorElement and SVGAElement
interface mixin HTMLOrSVGAnchorElement {
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString hreflang;
  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString type;

  [CEReactions] attribute DOMString text;
};
```


Currently SVG is defined to reflect href content attribute to baseVal IDL attribute. It doesn't look like it is defined in super details but it is at https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/types.html#InterfaceSVGURIReference and https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/types.html#InterfaceSVGAnimatedString
